<h1><a name="_Toc434907435">27.02    PURPOSE - GENERAL PROVISIONS</a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.02.010     Purpose.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.02.015     Relationship to Comprehensive Plan
and Growth Management Act.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.02.020     General provisions.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.02.030     Insufficient funds charge –
discretionary requirement of cashier's check, credit card payment, trust
account – acceptance of purchase orders from government agencies.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.02.040     Fee waivers – requirements – filing
– written decision – appeals – limits on challenges.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.02.050     Fee assessment (in effect until
January 1, 2027).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.02.050     Fee assessment (in effect January
1, 2027, and thereafter).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.02.055     Agricultural buildings or
activities – charged fifty percent of fees in title for processing, review or
inspection of applications.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.02.060     Refunds (in effect until January 1,
2027).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.02.060     Refunds (in effect January 1, 2027,
and thereafter).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.02.100     General service fee.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.02.110     Contract fees.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.02.201     Fee schedule - availability.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.02.202     Surcharge on fees established in
K.C.C. chapters 27.06 and 27.10 - use - exceptions - dates for surcharge -
removal of surcharge by ordinance (in effect until January 1, 2027).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.02.210     Deposits.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.02.220     Disaster response expenditures.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.02.230     Regional motor sports facility
master planning demonstration project – compensation to county - costs - rates.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          27.02.010 
Purpose.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The purpose of this title is:  to prescribe equitable and
reasonable fees and fee collection, consistent with RCW 82.02.020, for permits
and other county approvals to cover the cost to the county of processing
applications, inspecting and reviewing plans, or preparing required detailed
statements by the department of local services, permitting division and road
services division, and the department of natural resources and parks, and to
prescribe school impact fees to cover the proportionate share of the cost of
new school facilities needed to serve new growth and development.  (<a
name="_Hlk57720485">Ord. 19857 § 2, 2024:  Ord. 19195 § 2, 2020:  Ord. 18791 §
201, 2018:  </a>Ord. 17682 § 2, 2013:  Ord. 13332 § 55, 1998:  Ord. 10662 § 42,
1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          <b>27.02.015  Relationship
to Comprehensive Plan and Growth Management Act.</b>  This title of the King
County Code is hereby enacted to be consistent and implement the comprehensive
plan in accordance with RCW 36.70A.  (Ord. 11623 § 1, 1994).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          27.02.020  General
provisions.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  This chapter deals with provisions general to the
administration of this title and includes fee waivers, fee assessments, refunds
and general services.  (Ord. 18822 § 2, 2018:  Ord. 17682 § 3, 2013:  Ord.
17224 § 2, 2011:  Ord. 11141 § 37, 1993:  Ord. 10662 § 43, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          27.02.030  Insufficient
funds charge – discretionary requirement of cashier's check, credit card
payment, trust account – acceptance of purchase orders from government agencies.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          A.  The
department shall charge an insufficient funds charge of thirty-five dollars.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          B.  The director
shall have the discretion to require payment of fees by cashier’s check or
credit card by customers with a history of payments rejected for insufficient
funds.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          C.  The director
shall have the discretion to establish a trust account into which an applicant
may deposit funds to be held by the department until spent for services
requested by the applicant.  Interest shall not be paid on funds held in
trust.  Unused funds held in trust shall be returned to applicants within
thirty days of written request for release.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          D.  The director
shall have the discretion to accept purchase orders from government agencies in
lieu of fee payment at application.  When a purchase order is accepted, fees
shall be paid by the due date indicated by the invoice from the department.  (Ord.
18822 § 3, 2018:  Ord. 16959 § 2, 2010:  Ord. 15957 § 1, 2007:  Ord. 15946 § 3,
2007:  Ord. 10662 § 44, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          27.02.040  Fee
waivers – requirements – filing – written decision – appeals – limits on
challenges.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          </span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>A 
The director shall have the discretion to waive all or a portion of the fees
administered by the department and required pursuant to this title, provided,
the waiver is warranted in the director's judgment.  A fee shall be waived if
one or more of the following conditions applies to the service for which the
fee was assessed:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            1.  The
service was not performed;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>            2.  The service is duplicative;
that is, a service of similar body of work was already performed and fees were
collected for that service;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
lang=X-NONE style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>            3.  The service is not required for permit approval;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
lang=X-NONE style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>            4.  The service was based on a professional or processing
error caused by the department;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
lang=X-NONE style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>            5.  The service was in response to a natural disaster as
declared by the </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>e</span><span lang=X-NONE style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>xecutive in accordance
with K.C.C. 12.52.030; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
lang=X-NONE style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>            </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>6</span><span lang=X-NONE style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>.  The service was in
response to a public health or safety emergency, for which in the judgement of
the director the public benefit of permitting services exceeds the fee for the
services.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
lang=X-NONE style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>          B.  An applicant must file a fee waiver request in writing no
later than twenty-one days after final approval of the permit by the
department.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
lang=X-NONE style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>          C.  Any fee waiver decision shall be in writing and shall
state a compelling need or public purpose to be served by the waiver, if
granted.  The need or purpose must be consistent with standards established in
subsection A. of this section and under K.C.C. chapter 2.98.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
lang=X-NONE style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>          D.  </span><span lang=X-NONE style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>The director's fee waiver decision is final
unless the applicant then files with the director a statement of appeal,
together with the required appeal fee, and complies with the appeal provisions
in K.C.C. 20.22.080.  The applicant may appeal a fee waiver decision only if
the director has denied all or a portion of the applicant's request.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
lang=X-NONE style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>          E.  </span><span lang=X-NONE style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>In an appeal of a fee waiver decision, the
burden is on the applicant to prove that the particular fee was unreasonable or
inconsistent with this title.  If the applicant fails to meet that burden, the
examiner shall affirm the decision of the director.  If the examiner determines
that a particular fee was unreasonable or inconsistent with the provisions of
this title, the examiner shall modify the fee, order the department to modify
the fee in accordance with the examiner's ruling or provide such other relief
as reasonably necessary.  If the examiner determines that the applicant is the
substantially prevailing party, the department shall waive and refund the
appeal fee.  The examiner's decision is final.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
lang=X-NONE style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          F.
In an appeal under this section, the applicant may only challenge the
department's application of the development permit fees provided for in this
title to the applicant's permit and approval.  The applicant may not challenge
in an appeal under this section the development permit fees in this title.</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>  </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>(Ord.
19529 § 2, 2022:  Ord. 18822 § 4, 2018:  Ord. 15946 § 4, 2007:  Ord. 13332 §
56, 1998:  Ord. 11141 § 38, 1993:  Ord. 10662 § 45, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          27.02.050  Fee
assessment (in effect until January 1, 2027*).</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          A.  Unless
otherwise required by this title, fees shall be assessed at the fee rate in
effect at the time the application for a permit or decision is deemed complete
or the request for other service is accepted by the department, but only if the
application is approved or permit is issued within twelve months of the date
that the application is deemed complete or otherwise accepted by the
department.  For services rendered after twelve months from the date the
application is deemed complete or otherwise accepted by the department, any
additional fees shall be assessed based on the rates in current effect.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
lang=X-NONE style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          <span
style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>B.  Fees for application screening are due at the
time of application submittal.</span></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
lang=X-NONE style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>          C.  Fees for application review are due at the time of
application acceptance.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
lang=X-NONE style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          <span
style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>D.  </span>Fees for expedited review are due when
an expedited review request is accepted by the department.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
lang=X-NONE style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          E. 
Fees owed for the resubmittal of plans or applications are due at the time of
resubmittal.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
lang=X-NONE style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          <span
style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>F.  </span>Fees for permits, inspection, or
monitoring are due at the time of permit issuance.  The director may grant
exceptions in cases where the basis as prescribed in this title for calculating
fees for a permit, inspection, or monitoring was amended after an application
was completed but before permit issuance.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
lang=X-NONE style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          <span
style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>G.  </span>Fees for reinspection of construction
work or site conditions are due by the date indicated on the department's
invoice or before final construction approval, whichever is earlier, and shall
be assessed at the fee rate in effect at the time of reinspection.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
lang=X-NONE style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          <span
style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>H.  Unless otherwise allowed by this title, the
department shall not accept payment of fees before fees are due.</span></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=X-NONE
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          I. 
</span><span lang=X-NONE style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
color:#23221F'>Changes in the ownership of an application or permit shall not
revoke the fees incurred by the application or permit, or the requirement to
post financial guarantees for permitted construction.</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:#23221F'>  </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>(Ord.
20021 § 2 (in effect until January 1, 2027):  Ord. 19857 § 3, 2024:  Ord. 18822
§ 5, 2018:  Ord. 16959 § 3, 2010:  Ord. 10662 § 46, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>*Reviser's note:  Sections
2 through 33 of this ordinance expire January 1, 2027.  (Ordinance 20021 § 36).</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          27.02.050  Fee
assessment (in effect January 1, 2027, and thereafter*).</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          A.  Unless
otherwise required by this title, fees shall be assessed at the fee rate in
effect at the time the application for a permit or decision is deemed complete
or the request for other service is accepted by the department, but only if the
application is approved or permit is issued within twelve months of the date
that the application is deemed complete or otherwise accepted by the
department.  For services rendered after twelve months from the date the
application is deemed complete or otherwise accepted by the department, any
additional fees shall be assessed based on the rates in current effect.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
lang=X-NONE style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          <span
style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>B.  Fees for application review are due upon
application acceptance.</span></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
lang=X-NONE style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          <span
style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>C.  </span>Fees for expedited review are due when
an expedited review request is accepted by the department.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
lang=X-NONE style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          D. 
Fees owed for the resubmittal of plans or applications are due at the time of
resubmittal.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
lang=X-NONE style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          <span
style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>E.  </span>Fees for permits, inspection or
monitoring are due upon permit issuance.  The director may grant exceptions in
cases where the basis as prescribed in this title for calculating fees for a
permit, inspection or monitoring was amended after an application was completed
but before permit issuance.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
lang=X-NONE style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          <span
style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>F.  </span>Fees for reinspection of construction
work or site conditions are due by the date indicated on the department's
invoice or before final construction approval, whichever is earlier, and shall
be assessed at the fee rate in effect at the time of reinspection.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
lang=X-NONE style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          <span
style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>G.  Unless otherwise allowed by this title, the
department shall not accept payment of fees before fees are due.</span></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=X-NONE
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          H. 
</span><span lang=X-NONE style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
color:#23221F'>Changes in the ownership of an application or permit shall not
revoke the fees incurred by the application or permit, or the requirement to
post financial guarantees for permitted construction.</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:#23221F'>  </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>(Ord.
20021 § 2 (expired January 1, 2027):  Ord. 19857 § 3, 2024:  Ord. 18822 § 5,
2018:  Ord. 16959 § 3, 2010:  Ord. 10662 § 46, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>*Reviser's note:  Sections
2 through 33 of this ordinance expire January 1, 2027.  (Ordinance 20021 § 36).</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-indent:.5in'><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>27.02.055 
Agricultural buildings or activities – charged fifty percent of fees in title
for processing, review or inspection of applications.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Processing,
review or inspection of applications or permits for agricultural buildings or
activities shall be charged fifty percent of the fees listed in this title. 
This section does not apply to processing, review, or inspections related to
applications or permits required for any use related to a product excluded from
the definition of &quot;agricultural product&quot; under RCW 82.04.213.  (Ord. 18385
§ 38, 2016).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          27.02.060  Refunds
(in effect until January 1, 2027*).</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          </span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>A. 
Fees for preapplication service requests or application screening are not
refundable once paid by the applicant.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          B.  Fees for
review of an application are refundable in proportion to the amount of work
performed as of the date of application withdrawal or cancellation if, within
sixty days after the date that fees were paid, the applicant in writing
withdraws, cancels, or otherwise terminates the application and requests a
refund.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          C.  Fees for
inspection of a permit are refundable if, prior to expiration of the permit,
the permit holder in writing withdraws, cancels, or otherwise terminates the
permit and requests a refund before commencing construction or land disturbing
activity authorized by the permit.  Permit fees shall not be refunded after
construction or land disturbing activity has commenced.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          D.  The
department shall refund a fee that has been paid but waived, or if other fees
are owed, apply the payment to outstanding fees.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          E.  Fees shall be
refunded to the applicant of record.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          F.  The
department shall waive and refund the fee for filing an appeal when an
applicant is the substantially prevailing party in an administrative appeal.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          G.  Fees paid in
accordance with this title shall not be refunded except as provided for in this
title.  (Ord. 20021 § 3 (in effect until January 1, 2027):  Ord. 19195 § 3, 2020: 
Ord. 18822 § 6, 2018:  Ord. 17923 § 2, 2014:  Ord. 17224 § 3, 2011:  Ord. 16959
§ 4, 2010:  Ord. 13332 § 57, 1998:  Ord. 10662 § 47, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>*Reviser's note:  Sections
2 through 33 of this ordinance expire January 1, 2027.  (Ordinance 20021 § 36).</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          27.02.060 
Refunds (in effect January 1, 2027, and thereafter*).</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          </span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>A. 
Fees for processing or review of an application are refundable in proportion to
the amount of work performed as of the date of application withdrawal or
cancellation if, within sixty days after the date that fees were paid, the
applicant in writing withdraws, cancels or otherwise terminates the application
and requests a refund.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          B.  Fees for
processing or inspection of a permit are refundable if, prior to expiration of
the permit, the permit holder in writing withdraws, cancels or otherwise
terminates the permit and requests a refund before commencing construction or
land disturbing activity authorized by the permit.  Permit fees shall not be
refunded after construction or land disturbing activity has commenced.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          C.  The
department shall refund a fee that has been paid but waived, or if other fees
are owed, apply the payment to outstanding fees.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          D.  Fees shall be
refunded to the applicant of record.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          E.  The
department shall waive and refund the fee for filing an appeal when an
applicant is the substantially prevailing party in an administrative appeal.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          F.  Development
permit and environmental review fees shall not be refunded except as provided
for in this title.  (Ord. 20021 § 3 (expired January 1, 2027):  Ord. 19195 § 3,
2020:  Ord. 18822 § 6, 2018:  Ord. 17923 § 2, 2014:  Ord. 17224 § 3, 2011: 
Ord. 16959 § 4, 2010:  Ord. 13332 § 57, 1998:  Ord. 10662 § 47, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>*Reviser's note:  Sections
2 through 33 of this ordinance expire January 1, 2027.  (Ordinance 20021 § 36).</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          27.02.100  Fee
for services without specified fees.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  For a service not listed
in this title, the department may charge a fee for the most comparable service
listed in this title, or may charge a fee to recover the actual cost of
providing services for which fees are not otherwise listed in this title or for
which the fees listed in this title do not recover the actual cost.  (Ord. 18822
§ 7, 2018:  Ord. 17682 § 5, 2013:  Ord. 17453 § 3, 2012:  Ord. 17224 § 6,
2011:  Ord. 14683 § 36, 2003:  Ord. 13996 § 11, 2000:  [Ord. 13664 § 12, 1999,
repealed by Ord. 13996 § 13, 2000]:  Ord. 13332 § 61, 1998:  Ord. 11141 § 40,
1993).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          27.02.110 
Contract fees.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  In addition to the fees required for review, processing
or inspection by the department, the department is authorized to charge an
applicant for the cost charged by a department-hired contractor that reviews or
processes an application, provides on-call permitting assistance when permit
volumes or staffing levels change rapidly, in accordance with RCW
36.70B.160(1)(d), or provides inspection or other required services. (Ord.
19857 § 4, 2024:  Ord. 17923 § 4, 2014:  Ord. 17453 § 4, 2012: Ord. 11141 § 41,
1993).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'>          <b>27.02.201  Fee schedule
- availability.  </b>The department shall make available for inspection, review
and copying by the public a fee schedule of its current fees in both written
and electronic form.  The department shall also post the fee schedule on the
department’s website.  (Ord. 16959 <span style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span>
13, 2010).</p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'>&nbsp;</p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'>          <b>27.02.202  Surcharge on
fees established in K.C.C. chapters 27.06 and 27.10 - use - exceptions - dates
for surcharge - removal of surcharge by ordinance (in effect until January 1,
2027*).</b></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'>          A.  Except as otherwise
provided in subsection B. of this section, this ordinance has added a surcharge
of three and five tenths percent on all fees established in K.C.C. chapters
27.06 and 27.10.  The surcharge shall only be used to fund:</p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'>            1.  Replacement or
upgrade of the permitting software or information systems used by the
department.</p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'>            2.  The department's
undesignated fund balance for working capital in order to achieve an
undesignated fund balance of forty-five days of operating and maintenance
expenses.</p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'>          B.  The following fees
shall not be subject to the surcharge established in subsection A. of this
section:</p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'>            1.  Road variance review
under K.C.C. 27.10.070.A.1.;</p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'>            2.  Stormwater
engineering and document review under K.C.C. 27.10.082;</p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'>            3.  Road engineering
review under K.C.C. 27.10.084;</p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'>            4.  Road
constructability review under K.C.C. 27.10.085;</p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'>            5.  Stormwater facility
constructability review under K.C.C. 27.10.087;</p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'>            6.  Floodplain permits
established in K.C.C. 27.10.147;</p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'>            7.  Stormwater facility
site inspection and pre-site work engineering meetings under K.C.C. 27.10.385;</p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'>            8.  Road construction
inspection and pre-site work engineering meetings under K.C.C. 27.10.395; </p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'>            9.  Financial guarantee
processing, monitoring, extension, and administration under K.C.C. 27.10.570;
and</p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'>            10.  Title elimination
in K.C.C. 27.10.580.D.</p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'>          C.  The surcharge applies
to fees charged between January 1, 2026, and December 31, 2027.  An ordinance
will be required to remove the surcharge from the fees to which it applies. 
(Ord. 20021 § 4 (expires January 1, 2027)).</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>*Reviser's note:  Sections
2 through 33 of this ordinance expire January 1, 2027.  (Ordinance 20021 § 36).</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          <b>27.02.210 
Deposits.</b>  The department may require a deposit for incremental fees for
requested or required services at the time an application is accepted or a
permit is issued or extended.  The deposit shall not exceed the estimated cost
of the services for which the deposit is collected.  Interest shall not be paid
on moneys held on deposit.  Moneys remaining on deposit upon completion or
cancellation of service shall be refunded to the applicant.  (Ord. 18822 § 8, 2018: 
Ord. 17682 § 6, 2013:  Ord. 17224 § 12, 2011:  Ord. 14683 § 39, 2003:  Ord.
13332 § 63, 1998).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          <b>27.02.220 
Disaster response expenditures.</b>  Expenditures drawn from the permitting division
fund for disaster response, which are not recovered through the assessment of
fees or reimbursement from the Federal Emergency Management Administration
(FEMA), shall be reimbursed to the permitting division fund by the current
expense fund within twelve months of when the expenses were incurred.  (Ord. 18791
§ 202, 2018:  Ord. 17420 § 130, 2012:  Ord. 14238 § 32, 2001).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          27.02.230 
Regional motor sports facility master planning demonstration project –
compensation to county – costs – rates.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          A.  The
application for a master planning demonstration project under K.C.C. 21A.55.105
shall be subject to the fee provisions of this title.  King County shall be
compensated for all costs incurred by King County related to the review and
monitoring of the demonstration project, including, but not limited to, costs
for the:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            1.  Review of
the master planning application;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            2.  Review of
environmental documents submitted to the department by the consultant selected
in accordance with Ordinance 17287, Section 5;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            3. 
Preparation and issuance of the department-recommended development and
operating agreement;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4.  Issuance
of public notices;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            5.  Conduct of
meetings;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.  Response
to public inquiries related specifically to such notices and meetings; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            7.  Monitoring
of the approved development and operating agreement.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          B.  The review
costs for permit applications and studies related to specific development
proposals consistent with the development and operating agreement shall be
governed by this title.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          C.  The costs
from the consultant selected in accordance with Ordinance 17287, Section 5, and
billed to the department shall be paid by the applicant and shall be governed
by this title.  (Ord. 17682 § 7, 2013:   Ord. 17287 § 3, 2012).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc321750500"></a><a name="_Toc434907436">27.04    DEFINITIONS</a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.04.0005   Definitions – application.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.04.001     Agricultural activity.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.04.002     Agricultural building.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.04.003     Building official.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.04.004     Closed record hearing.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.04.005     Department.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.04.010     Development permits.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.04.015     Director.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.04.025     Impact fee.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.04.028     Environmental review.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.04.040     Permit fee.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.04.047     Substantial prevailing party.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.04.050     Valuation.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          <b>27.04.0005 
Definitions – application.</b>  </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>The definitions in this chapter apply to this
title unless the context clearly requires otherwise.  <span style='letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>(Ord. 18385 § 39, 2016).</span></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          <b>27.04.001 
Agricultural activity.</b></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          A.  Located on
an existing farm on RA-zoned property for which the property owner has a
current farm plan developed in conjunction with the King Conservation District
or on lands within the agricultural production district; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          B.  Related to
the following agricultural purposes:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            1.  The
storage, maintenance or repair of farm machinery and equipment;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            2.  The
raising, harvesting and selling of crops;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            3.  The
feeding, breeding, management and sale of, or the produce of, livestock,
poultry, fur-bearing animals or honeybees;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4.  Dairying
and the sale of dairy products;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            5.  Any other
agricultural or horticultural use or animal husbandry, or any combination
thereof, including the preparation, storage, processing or sale of agricultural
products raised on the farm for human use and animal use;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6. 
Processing, treatment, packaging, and sale of agricultural products;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            7.  Stabling
or training equines; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            8.  Equine
riding lessons and training clinics.  (Ord. 17224 § 13, 2011).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          <b>27.04.002 
Agricultural building.</b>  &quot;Agricultural building&quot; means a
structure, other than a dwelling, that is:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          A.  Located on
an existing farm on RA-zoned property for which the property owner has a
current farm plan developed in conjunction with the King Conservation District
or on lands within the agricultural production district; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          B.  Used in the
operation of the farm for:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            1.  The
storage, maintenance or repair of farm machinery and equipment;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            2.  The
raising, harvesting and selling of crops;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            3.  The
feeding, breeding, management and sale of, or the produce of, livestock,
poultry, fur-bearing animals or honeybees;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4.  Dairying
and the sale of dairy products;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            5.  Any other
agricultural or horticultural use or animal husbandry, or any combination
thereof, including the preparation, storage, processing, or sale of
agricultural products raised on the farm for human use and animal use;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6. 
Processing, treatment, packaging, and sale of agricultural products;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            7.  Stabling
or training equines; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            8.  Equine
riding lessons and training clinics.  (Ord. 17224 § 14, 2011).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          <b>27.04.003 
Building official.</b>  &quot;Building official&quot; means the department of local
services permitting division manager or designee.  (Ord. 18791 § 203, 2018: 
Ord. 17420 § 131, 2012:  Ord. 13332 § 14, 1998).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          <b>27.04.004  Closed record hearing.</b> 
&quot;Closed record hearing&quot; means an administrative appeal to the hearing
examiner of a departmental decision when the appeal is on the record with no
new evidence or information allowed to be submitted and only appeal argument
allowed.  The record shall consist solely of a complete set of the documents
relating to the facts of the department's decision.  (<span style='letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>Ord. 16026 § 5, 2008).</span></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          27.04.005 
Department.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  &quot;Department&quot; means the department of local
services or its successor.  (Ord. 18791 § 204, 2018:  Ord. 17420 § 132, 2012: 
Ord. 14683 § 6, 2003:  Ord. 10662 § 51, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          27.04.010 
Development permits.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  &quot;Development permits&quot; mean all permits,
reviews, and approvals administered by the department of local services,
permitting division, including, but not limited to, right-of-way use permits,
grading permits, building permits, fire code permits, subdivisions, short
subdivisions, binding site plans, planned unit developments, zoning permits,
master plan development permits, current use permits, boundary line
adjustments, and environmental review and shoreline permits.  (Ord. 18791 § 205,
2018:  Ord. 17420 § 133, 2012:  Ord. 16959 § 14, 2010:  Ord. 10662 § 53, 1992: 
Ord. 8330 § 31, 1987).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          27.04.015 
Director.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  &quot;Director&quot; means the department of local
services permitting division manager or designee.  (Ord. 18791 § 206, 2018: 
Ord. 18683 § 66, 2018:  Ord. 17420 § 134, 2012:  Ord. 10662 § 52, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          27.04.025  Impact
fee.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  &quot;Impact fee&quot; means a payment of money
authorized by state law and county ordinance to be imposed upon development as
a condition of development approval to pay for public facilities needed to
serve new growth and development.  Impact fees include but are not limited to
roads mitigation payment fees and school impact fees.  &quot;Impact fees&quot;
do not include fees imposed to cover the costs of processing applications,
inspecting and reviewing plans or other information required to be submitted
for purpose of evaluation of an application, or inspecting or monitoring
development activity.  (Ord. 10162 § 22, 1991).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          27.04.028  Environmental
review.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  &quot;Environmental review&quot; means all permits,
reviews, and approvals administered pursuant to K.C.C. 20.44.  (Ord. 10662 §
50, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          27.04.040 
Permit fee.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  &quot;Permit fee&quot; means a payment of money imposed
upon development as a condition of application for or approval of development
to cover the costs of processing applications, inspecting and reviewing plans
or other information required to be submitted for purpose of evaluation of an
application, or inspecting or monitoring development activity.  (Ord. 10162 §
23, 1991).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          27.04.047 Substantial prevailing
party.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'> 
A permit applicant is the &quot;substantial prevailing party&quot; in an appeal
under this title if the hearing examiner orders a reduction of the fee
estimate, estimate revision or billings that is fifty percent or more of the
cumulative sum that the applicant disputed before the examiner.  Otherwise, the
department is the &quot;substantial prevailing party.&quot;  (<span
style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Ord. 16026 § 6, 2008).</span></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          27.04.050 
Valuation.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  &quot;Valuation&quot; means the determination of value
made by the building official or the building official's designee using current
valuation tables published by the International Code Council or other current
nationally recognized standards.  The valuation includes the total value of all
construction work for which the permit is issued, including all finish work,
painting, roofing, electrical, plumbing, heating, ventilation and air
conditioning, elevators, fire systems and any other permanent fixtures.  (Ord.
17682 § 8, 2013:  Ord. 16959 § 15, 2010:  Ord. 15957 § 5, 2007:  Ord. 13996 §
2, 2000:  [Ord. 13664 § 3, 1999, repealed by Ord. 13996, § 13, 2000]:  Ord.
13332 § 15, 1998).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc321750501"></a><a name="_Toc434907437">27.06    PREAPPLICATION
AND COUNTER SERVICE FEES</a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.06.005     Purpose.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.06.010     Preapplication conferences - credit
- presubmittal project review - zoning certification letters (in effect until
January 1, 2027).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.06.010     Preapplication conferences - credit
- presubmittal project review - zoning certification letters (in effect January
1, 2027, and thereafter).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          27.06.005 
Purpose.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The purpose of this chapter is to establish fees for
preapplication submittal services and processing.  (Ord. 18385 § 2, 2016:  Ord.
17682 § 9, 2013:  Ord. 17453 § 8, 2012:  Ord. 17224 § 15, 2011:  Ord. 14683 §
40, 2003:  Ord. 13332 § 3, 1998).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          <b>27.06.010 
Preapplication conferences - credit - presubmittal project review - zoning
certification letters (in effect until January 1, 2027*).</b></span></p>

<table class=MsoNormalTable border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0
 style='margin-left:41.4pt;border-collapse:collapse'>
 <tr>
  <td width=569 colspan=3 valign=top style='width:426.6pt;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
  font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>A.  A fee shall be
  charged for preapplication services as follows:</span></p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td width=40 valign=top style='width:30.15pt;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
  font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  1.</span></p>
  </td>
  <td width=405 valign=top style='width:303.6pt;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
  font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Preapplication
  conference:  already built construction for residential use</span></p>
  </td>
  <td width=124 valign=top style='width:92.85pt;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal align=right style='text-align:right'><span
  style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>$1,452.00</span></p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td width=40 valign=top style='width:30.15pt;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
  font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  2.</span></p>
  </td>
  <td width=405 valign=top style='width:303.6pt;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
  font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Preapplication
  conference:  already built construction for commercial use</span></p>
  </td>
  <td width=124 valign=top style='width:92.85pt;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal align=right style='text-align:right'><span
  style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>$5,809.00</span></p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td width=40 valign=top style='width:30.15pt;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
  font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  3.</span></p>
  </td>
  <td width=405 valign=top style='width:303.6pt;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
  font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Preapplication
  conference:  other development type, per county staff participant</span></p>
  </td>
  <td width=124 valign=top style='width:92.85pt;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal align=right style='text-align:right'><span
  style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>
  <p class=MsoNormal align=right style='text-align:right'><span
  style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>$1,452.00</span></p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td width=40 valign=top style='width:30.15pt;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
  font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  4.</span></p>
  </td>
  <td width=405 valign=top style='width:303.6pt;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
  font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Cancellation of a
  conference without notification before its scheduled start time or failure to
  attend</span></p>
  </td>
  <td width=124 valign=top style='width:92.85pt;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal align=right style='text-align:right'><span
  style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>
  <p class=MsoNormal align=right style='text-align:right'><span
  style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>$57.00</span></p>
  </td>
 </tr>
</table>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          B.  The total preapplication
conference fee under subsection A.1. and 2. of this section shall be credited
against any required application or permit fees for a subsequent permit
application to address work commenced without permits, but only if the
subsequent permit application is filed within one hundred eighty days of the
preapplication conference or within sixty days of public health department or
other agency approval required for a complete development permit application.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          C.  Twenty
percent of the preapplication conference fee due for one county staff person
according to subsection A.3. of this section shall be paid when the request for
a preapplication conference is submitted.  The payment received shall be
credited toward the total preapplication conference fees due when the request
is accepted by the county.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          D.  The fee for
a zoning certification letter confirming an existing zoning designation or
development rights is four hundred eighty-three dollars.  The fee for zoning
certification requiring historic research or review of other information is one
thousand four hundred fifty-two dollars.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          E.  A fee of seven
hundred twenty-six dollars shall be charged for each inspection of structures
for housing code compliance, damage from flood, storm, fire, or other natural
disaster, or for each site visit conducted before permit application.  (Ord. 20021
§ 5 (in effect until January 1, 2027):  Ord. 19857 § 5, 2024:  Ord. 19529 § 3,
2022:  Ord. 19195 § 4, 2020:  Ord. 18822 § 9, 2018:  Ord. 18791 § 207, 2018:  Ord.
18385 § 2, 2016:  Ord. 17923 § 7, 2014:  Ord. 17682 § 10, 2013:  Ord. 17453 §
9, 2012:  Ord. 17224 § 16, 2011:  Ord. 16959 § 16, 2010:  Ord. 14683 § 41,
2003:  Ord. 13332 § 4, 1998).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>*Reviser's note:  Sections
2 through 33 of this ordinance expire January 1, 2027.  (Ordinance 20021 § 36).</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          <b>27.06.010 
Preapplication conferences - credit - presubmittal project review - zoning
certification letters (in effect January 1, 2027, and thereafter*).</b></span></p>

