-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.10.560     Address or road name changes
request - no site visit (in effect January 1, 2027, and thereafter).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.10.570     Processing, monitoring, extending
and administering the default of financial guarantees.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.10.580     Permit processing, clerical
services, contractor certification, title elimination, permit extension, review
of resubmitted plans and permit revisions, expedited review, and after-hours
inspection (in effect until January 1, 2027).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        27.10.580     Permit processing, clerical
services, contractor certification, title elimination, permit extension, review
of resubmitted plans and permit revisions, expedited review and after-hours
inspection (in effect January 1, 2027, and thereafter).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          27.10.010  Plan
review - applicability.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Plan review fees <span style='letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>shall compensate the department for the plan review necessary to
determine compliance with approved plans, adopted international codes and other
county regulations.  The fees shall be collected to compensate the department for
the review of:</span></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          A.  Commercial
and residential building permit applications under K.C.C. chapters 16.04, 16.78
and 17.04 and K.C.C. Titles 20 and 21A;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          B.  Grading and
clearing permit applications under K.C.C. chapter 16.82;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          C.  Shoreline
permit applications and exemptions under K.C.C. Title 25;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          D.  State
Environmental Policy Act compliance under K.C.C. chapter 20.44 ;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          E.  Critical areas
under K.C.C. chapter 21A.24;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          F.  Preliminary
and final subdivisions and short subdivisions under K.C.C. Title 19A;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          G.  Binding site
plan review under K.C.C. Title 19A;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          H.  Boundary
line adjustments under K.C.C. Title 19A;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          I.  Variance
requests, conditional use permits, zone reclassification requests, special use
permits and temporary use permits under K.C.C. Title 21A;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          J.  Right of way
use permits under K.C.C. Title 14; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          K.  Drainage
review under K.C.C. Title 9.  (Ord. 19485 § 209, 2022:  Ord. 17682 § 11, 2013: 
Ord. 16959 § 18, 2010:  Ord. 15957 § 8, 2007:  Ord. 13332 § 16, 1998).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=Normal>          <b>27.10.015  Application screening fee for certain
permits or approvals (in effect until January 1, 2027*).  </b><span
style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>An application screening fee of one hundred
twenty-six dollars shall be charged and paid at the time of application
submittal for a permit or approval that requires plan review and application
screening before the application is deemed complete.  (Ord. 20021 § 6 (expired
January 1, 2027)).</span></p>

<p class=Normal><span style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=Normal><b>*Reviser's note:  Sections 2 through 33 of this ordinance
expire January 1, 2027.  (Ordinance 20021 § 36).</b></p>

<p class=Normal><b>&nbsp;</b></p>

<p class=Normal>          <b>27.10.020  Plan review, including additions and
modifications – reviewing applications to construct or modify buildings,
structures, and equipment - resubmittal or revisions (in effect until January
1, 2027*).</b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          </span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>A.  Except as otherwise
provided in this section, plan review fees for <span style='letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>buildings and structures, including</span></span> <span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>construction,
additions, modifications, and equipment, shall be calculated using valuations
published by the International Code Council or other current nationally
recognized standards.  The building official shall establish the final
valuation.  Fees shall be based on the valuation established under this
subsection as follows:</span></p>

