<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          B.  Plan review
fees shall be charged for construction or modifications of buildings,
structures, and equipment as follows:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            1.  Electronic
communication antenna                                  $3,364.00</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            2.  Electronic
communication tower or pole                           $6,272.00</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            3.  Sign                                                                              $1,597.00</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4.  Portable
classroom, per group of three units or fraction thereof          $5,269.00</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            5.  Trail
bridge, per linear foot                                                   $42.00</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.  Building
change of use only                                               $970.00</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          C.  Each plan resubmittal
or revisions to an issued permit shall be charged a fraction of the original
building plan review fee proportionate to the changes from the original plan
submittal, as determined by the department.  (Ord. 20021 § 7 (in effect until
January 1, 2027):  Ord. 19857 § 6, 2024:  Ord. 19529 § 4, 2022:  Ord. 19195 § 5,
2020:  Ord. 18822 § 10, 2018:  Ord. 18385 § 3, 2016:  Ord. 17923 § 8, 2014:  Ord.
17682 § 12, 2013:  Ord. 17453 § 11, 2012:  Ord. 17224 § 19, 2011:  Ord. 16959 §
19, 2010:  Ord. 14683 § 42, 2003:  Ord. 13996 § 3, 2000:  [Ord. 13664 § 4,
1999, repealed by Ord. 13996, § 13, 2000]:  Ord. 13332 § 17, 1998).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>*Reviser's note:  Sections
2 through 33 of this ordinance expire January 1, 2027.  (Ordinance 20021 § 36).</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=Normal>          <b>27.10.020  Plan review, including additions and
modifications – reviewing applications to construct or modify buildings,
structures, and equipment - resubmittal or revisions (in effect January 1,
2027, and thereafter*).</b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          </span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>A.  Except as otherwise
provided in this section, fees for the <span style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>review
of buildings and structures, including additions, modifications and mechanical
equipment, shall be calculated using valuations published by the International
Code Council or other current nationally recognized standards.  The building
official shall establish the final valuation.  The fee charged shall be based
on the valuation established under this subsection as follows:</span></span></p>

