authorization.  Building and site inspections shall be charged the regular fees
adopted by this title.  (Ord. 20021 § 31 (expired January 1, 2027):  Ord. 19857
§ 29, 2024:  Ord. 19529 § 27, 2022:  Ord. 19195 § 34, 2020:  Ord. 18822 § 39,
2018:  Ord. 18385 § 33, 2016:  Ord. 17923 § 40, 2014:  Ord. 17682 § 45, 2013: 
Ord. 17453 § 44, 2012:  Ord. 16959 § 45, 2010:  Ord. 14683 § 51, 2003:  Ord.
14683 § 33, 2003:  Ord. 13332 § 54, 1998).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>*Reviser's note:  Sections
2 through 33 of this ordinance expire January 1, 2027.  (Ordinance 20021 § 36).</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          27.10.560 
Address or road name changes requests - no site visit (in effect until January
1, 2027*).</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Requests for address or road name changes where no site
visit is required shall be charged one hundred ninety-two dollars per address
affected by the requested change.  (Ord. 20021 § 32 (in effect until January 1,
2027):  Ord. 19857 § 30, 2024:  Ord. 19529 § 28, 2022:  Ord. 19195 § 35, 2020: 
Ord. 18822 § 40, 2018:  Ord. 18385 § 34, 2016:  Ord. 17923 § 41, 2014:  Ord.
17682 § 46, 2013).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>*Reviser's note:  Sections
2 through 33 of this ordinance expire January 1, 2027.  (Ordinance 20021 § 36).</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          27.10.560 
Address or road name changes requests - no site visit (in effect January 1,
2027, and thereafter*).</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Requests for address or road name
changes where no site visit is required shall be charged one hundred
sixty-eight dollars per address affected by the requested change.  (Ord. 20021
§ 32 (expired January 1, 2027):  Ord. 19857 § 30, 2024:  Ord. 19529 § 28,
2022:  Ord. 19195 § 35, 2020:  Ord. 18822 § 40, 2018:  Ord. 18385 § 34, 2016: 
Ord. 17923 § 41, 2014:  Ord. 17682 § 46, 2013).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>*Reviser's note:  Sections
2 through 33 of this ordinance expire January 1, 2027.  (Ordinance 20021 § 36).</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          <b>27.10.570 
Processing, monitoring, extending and administering the default of financial
guarantees.  </b>Fees shall be charged as follows for processing, monitoring,
extending and administering the default of financial guarantees:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          A.       Standard monitoring of maintenance and
defect guarantees for completed installation</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            1.     Inspection of stormwater facilities -
small                      $4,107.00</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            2.     Inspection of stormwater facilities -
medium                  $4,997.00</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            3.     Inspection of stormwater facilities -
large                      $7,649.00</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4.     Reinspection of stormwater facilities,
each                      $770.00</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            5.     Inspection of road improvements -
small                       $4,107.00</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.     Inspection of road improvements -
medium                   $4,997.00</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            7.     Inspection of road improvements -
large                       $7,649.00</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            8.     Reinspection of road improvements,
each                       $770.00</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            9.     Inspection or reinspection of critical
area mitigation, landscaping,</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                    street or significant trees, or
recreation facilities per site visit          $375.00</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          B.       Extended monitoring of maintenance and
defect guarantees -</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                    additional year</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            1.     Stormwater facilities                                                   $1,968.00</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            2.     Road improvements                                                   $1,968.00</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          C.       Administering default of financial
guarantees - annual fee</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            1.     Road improvements                                                   $4,424.00</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            2.     Stormwater facilities                                                   $4,424.00</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>(Ord. 19195 § 36, 2020:  Ord.
18822 § 41, 2018:  Ord. 18791 § 209, 2018:  Ord. 18385 § 35, 2016:  Ord. 17923
§ 42, 2014:  Ord. 17682 § 47, 2013).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          27.10.580  Permit
processing, clerical services, contractor certification, title elimination,
permit extension, review of resubmitted plans and permit revisions, expedited
review, and after-hours inspection (in effect until January 1, 2027*).</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
Fees shall be charged for permit processing, clerical services, contractor
certification, title elimination, permit extension, review of resubmitted plans
and permit revisions, expedited review, and after-hours inspection as follows:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          A.  The
department may charge a fee for its actual cost of reissuing a public notice.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          B.  The
department may charge fees for clerical services unrelated to permits
including, but not limited to, making copies, scanning documents, notarizing
documents, gathering, preparing and publishing special request reports and
providing publications.  The fees shall be the actual cost to the department
and shall be collected at the time services are requested.  The department
shall publish a schedule of these fees on the internet and in the public areas
of its offices.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          C.  The fee for
annual certification of a tank removal contractor shall be the minimum fee
amount in K.C.C 27.10.320.A.1.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          D.  The fee for
a title elimination is sixty dollars.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          E.  The fee for
extension of a permit shall be the minimum fee amount in K.C.C 27.10.320.A.1.,
except that the fee for extension of a single detached residence mechanical
installation permit shall be twenty-five percent of the minimum fee amount per
K.C.C. 27.10.320.A.1.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          F.  Unless
otherwise specified in this title, the review of resubmitted plans or revisions
to an issued building, fire or grading permit shall be charged a fee of
twenty-five percent of the original application fee.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          G.  The fee for
expedited review of project permit applications for projects that are
consistent with adopted development regulations, in accordance with RCW
36.70B.160(1)(a), shall be one hundred fifty percent of the regular review fee,
and shall be charged in lieu of the regular review fee in this title.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          H.  When
building or land use inspections outside regular business hours are required by
the construction schedule or otherwise requested by a permit holder, excluding
inspections for fireworks displays and other special events, the overtime labor
cost of county personnel shall be charged in addition to the regular inspection
fees.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          <u>I. 
Permits for a new single detached residence served by exempt domestic wells
shall be charged the following fees in accordance with RCW 90.94.030:</u></span></p>

<table class=MsoNormalTable border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0
 style='border-collapse:collapse;border:none'>
 <tr>
  <td width=397 valign=top style='width:297.9pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;
  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>           
  <u>1.  Washington state Department of Ecology</u></span></p>
  </td>
  <td width=193 valign=top style='width:144.9pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;
  border-left:none;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal><u><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>$350.00</span></u></p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td width=397 valign=top style='width:297.9pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;
  border-top:none;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>           
  <u>2.  King County</u></span></p>
  </td>
  <td width=193 valign=top style='width:144.9pt;border-top:none;border-left:
  none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;
  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal><u><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>$150.00</span></u></p>
  </td>
 </tr>
</table>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          <u>J. 
Development proposals on parcels with cultural resources shall be charged the
following fees for services provided by the King County historical preservation
program:</u></span></p>

<table class=MsoNormalTable border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0
 style='border-collapse:collapse;border:none'>
 <tr>
  <td width=397 valign=top style='width:297.9pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;
  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>           
  <u>1.  Screening for cultural resource</u></span></p>
  </td>
  <td width=193 valign=top style='width:144.9pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;
  border-left:none;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal><u><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>$150.00</span></u></p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td width=397 valign=top style='width:297.9pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;
  border-top:none;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>           
  <u>2.  Archeological review</u></span></p>
  </td>
  <td width=193 valign=top style='width:144.9pt;border-top:none;border-left:
  none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;
  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal><u><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>$450.00</span></u></p>
  </td>
 </tr>
</table>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  (Ord. 20021 § 33 (in
effect until January 1, 2027):  Ord. 19857 § 31, 2024:  Ord. 19529 § 29, 2022: 
Ord. 19276 § 14, 2021:  Ord. 19195 § 37, 2020:  Ord. 18822 § 42, 2018:  Ord. 18385
§ 36, 2016:  Ord. 17923 § 43, 2014:  Ord. 17682 § 48, 2013).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>*Reviser's note:  Sections
2 through 33 of this ordinance expire January 1, 2027.  (Ordinance 20021 § 36).</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          27.10.580  Permit
processing, clerical services, contractor certification, title elimination,
permit extension, review of resubmitted plans and permit revisions, expedited
review and after-hours inspection (in effect January 1, 2027, and thereafter*).</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
Fees shall be charged for permit processing, clerical services, contractor
certification, title elimination, permit extension, review of resubmitted plans
and permit revisions, expedited review and after-hours inspection as follows:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          A.  The
department may charge a fee for its actual cost of reissuing a public notice.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          B.  The
department may charge fees for clerical services unrelated to permits
including, but not limited to, making copies, scanning documents, notarizing
documents, gathering, preparing and publishing special request reports and
providing publications.  The fees shall be the actual cost to the department
and shall be collected at the time services are requested.  The department
shall publish a schedule of these fees on the internet and in the public areas
of its offices.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          C.  The fee for
annual certification of a tank removal contractor shall be the minimum fee
amount in K.C.C 27.10.320.A.1.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          D.  The fee for
a title elimination is sixty dollars.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          E.  The fee for
extension of a permit shall be the minimum fee amount in K.C.C 27.10.320.A.1.,
except that the fee for extension of a single family residential mechanical
installation permit shall be twenty-five percent of the minimum fee amount per
K.C.C. 27.10.320.A.1.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          F.  The fee for
the third or subsequent intake screening of an application submittal prior to
acceptance is fifty dollars for each screening.  Unless otherwise specified in
this title, the review of resubmitted plans or revisions to an issued building,
fire or grading permit shall be charged a fee of twenty-five percent of the
original application fee.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          G.  The fee for
expedited review of project permit applications for projects that are
consistent with adopted development regulations, in accordance with RCW
36.70B.160(1)(a), shall be one hundred fifty percent of the regular review fee,
and shall be charged in lieu of the regular review fee in this title.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          H.  When
building or land use inspections outside regular business hours are required by
the construction schedule or otherwise requested by a permit holder, excluding
inspections for fireworks displays and other special events, the overtime labor
cost of county personnel shall be charged in addition to the regular inspection
fees.  (Ord. 20021 § 33 (expired January 1, 2027):  Ord. 19857 § 31, 2024:  Ord.
19529 § 29, 2022:  Ord. 19276 § 14, 2021:  Ord. 19195 § 37, 2020:  Ord. 18822 §
42, 2018:  Ord. 18385 § 36, 2016:  Ord. 17923 § 43, 2014:  Ord. 17682 § 48,
2013).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>*Reviser's note:  Sections
2 through 33 of this ordinance expire January 1, 2027.  (Ordinance 20021 § 36).</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc321750504"></a><a name="_Toc434907439">27.44    SCHOOL IMPACT
FEES</a></h1>

<p class=tx><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=tx><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=tx><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          27.44.010      School
impact fees.</span></p>

<p class=tx><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=tx><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          27.44.010 
School impact fees.</span></b></p>

<p class=tx style='margin-left:.5in'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>A. 
The following school impact fees shall be assessed for the indicated types of
development:</span></p>

<table class=MsoNormalTable border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0
 style='margin-left:.95in;border-collapse:collapse'>
 <tr>
  <td width=264 valign=top style='width:2.75in;border:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;
  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=tx><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>SCHOOL DISTRICT</span></p>
  </td>
  <td width=155 valign=top style='width:116.1pt;border:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;
  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=tx align=left style='text-align:left'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>SINGLE
  DETACHED</span></p>
  <p class=tx align=left style='text-align:left'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>per
  dwelling unit</span></p>
  </td>
  <td width=103 valign=top style='width:77.4pt;border:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;
  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=tx align=left style='text-align:left'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>MULTIUNIT
  per dwelling unit</span></p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td width=264 valign=top style='width:2.75in;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=tx><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Auburn, No. 408</span></p>
  </td>
  <td width=155 valign=top style='width:116.1pt;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=tx align=right style='margin-right:42.95pt;text-align:right'><span
  style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>$8,003</span></p>
  </td>
  <td width=103 valign=top style='width:77.4pt;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=tx align=right style='text-align:right'><span style='font-family:
  "Arial",sans-serif'>$5,000</span></p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td width=264 valign=top style='width:2.75in;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
